{"kind":"request","text":"claude: build the notification dropdown hugh asked for twice (#8600 and #10248) and which was wrongly lost in the staleness cascade: turn the top bar's \"N for you\" counter into an affordance — a dropdown off the viewer's avatar listing the events addressed to or mentioning them, each linking to its thread. The original lane a3f62a52 and its whole chain (821479c5 withdrawn, 54897781 cancelled, refile e21eeb11 withdrawn) died with no live or satisfied replacement, and main's ui/src has no notification surface at all. Hugh authorized this revival today (2026-09-02) after a full review of the withdrawn backlog.\n\nTHE FEATURE. The existing \"N for you\" count becomes clickable: it opens a list of the viewer's addressed and mention events, newest first, each row naming the sender and first line and opening the thread on click; an empty state says plainly that nothing is addressed to the viewer; the count and list stay consistent with the projection the board already renders (no new server endpoint unless the existing views genuinely cannot supply the rows — if so, stop and report before implementing).\n\nPRIOR WORK. Finished work sat dormant at head dc61ffb0 on request/ui-notification-dropdown and was never merged; it predates the ratified two-screen UI. Judge revive-versus-rebuild yourself — check what survives against current main before rebuilding, and carry nothing that reintroduces since-fixed defects. If the event-addresses lane (my request 5da1e08b) lands first, link rows by those addresses rather than duplicating navigation.\n\nCONDITIONS: (1) the counter opens the list, rows open their threads, and the empty state renders — each covered by a UI test. (2) UI gates green at the exact head with the embed rebuilt (make ui; npm ci in a fresh worktree). (3) request/\u003cslug\u003e worktree with Rests-On this request; exact-head artifact for ui; independent review citing this request and original a3f62a52. (4) Layer 7 only, with the stop-and-report rule above for any server change.","body":{"conditions":"The for-you counter opens a dropdown listing addressed/mention events with thread links and a truthful empty state, each behavior covered by a UI test; UI gates green at the exact head with the embed rebuilt via make ui; exact-head artifact for ui published and independent review requested citing this request plus original a3f62a52; layer 7 only, stopping to report if a server change proves necessary.","to":"a5d35aa7e4799472a208663d7f024917442bd513929f9eccf450628ccf70095d"}}